1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,929
Meridian Home Comfort asked one question.

2
00:00:02,929 --> 00:00:05,869
Can an A I agent settle sixty to seventy-five

3
00:00:05,869 --> 00:00:08,875
percent of the calls a busy call center takes,

4
00:00:08,875 --> 00:00:11,358
and hand the rest to a person cleanly?

5
00:00:11,358 --> 00:00:13,449
To find out, we read every call,

6
00:00:13,449 --> 00:00:17,043
built the agent, and tested it on thirty-one scenarios.

7
00:00:17,043 --> 00:00:19,068
It's live on Railway right now.

8
00:00:19,068 --> 00:00:20,636
Here's how we got there,

9
00:00:20,636 --> 00:00:22,270
and what the numbers say.

10
00:00:23,123 --> 00:00:26,520
First, the drivers. We read all four hundred twenty

11
00:00:26,520 --> 00:00:27,652
calls end to end.

12
00:00:27,652 --> 00:00:29,717
A rule set strips filler turns,

13
00:00:29,717 --> 00:00:32,781
then labels what the caller wanted and how the

14
00:00:32,781 --> 00:00:35,978
human settled it. A second read of twenty random

15
00:00:35,978 --> 00:00:38,975
calls agreed with those labels on all twenty.

16
00:00:38,975 --> 00:00:42,306
The five drivers the agent can actually settle are

17
00:00:42,306 --> 00:00:44,637
booking, warranty, billing lookups,

18
00:00:44,637 --> 00:00:47,767
membership questions and existing appointments.

19
00:00:47,767 --> 00:00:51,364
Together that's sixty-five point two percent of calls,

20
00:00:51,364 --> 00:00:53,229
and it's our honest ceiling.

21
00:00:53,229 --> 00:00:56,759
Disputes, refunds, safety and commercial work go to a

22
00:00:56,759 --> 00:00:57,958
person, by design.

23
00:00:58,809 --> 00:01:00,822
Next, chunking and retrieval.

24
00:01:00,822 --> 00:01:04,571
Fourteen callers asked, I thought the membership was a

25
00:01:04,571 --> 00:01:08,111
hundred forty-nine dollars? That was the old price,

26
00:01:08,111 --> 00:01:10,888
and it still sits in the archive folder.

27
00:01:10,888 --> 00:01:12,485
So let's ask the agent.

28
00:01:12,485 --> 00:01:15,609
Every file in the knowledge base has a status

29
00:01:15,609 --> 00:01:18,802
in a manifest, and only the nine current files

30
00:01:18,802 --> 00:01:23,523
are indexed. Superseded, internal and placeholder files never become

31
00:01:23,523 --> 00:01:26,508
passages, so the old price can't come back.

32
00:01:26,508 --> 00:01:29,215
Each price-book row is its own passage,

33
00:01:29,215 --> 00:01:31,784
and the holiday image and the fee P D

34
00:01:31,784 --> 00:01:34,630
F are indexed from text a person checked.

35
00:01:34,630 --> 00:01:37,754
A small embedding model returns the top five.

36
00:01:37,754 --> 00:01:39,351
And there's the answer,

37
00:01:39,351 --> 00:01:40,670
with today's price.

38
00:01:41,522 --> 00:01:43,269
Now, how escalation works.

39
00:01:43,269 --> 00:01:46,563
Let's start fresh, and say we were charged twice.

40
00:01:46,563 --> 00:01:50,192
A billing dispute is something the agent never settles

41
00:01:50,192 --> 00:01:52,141
on its own. It doesn't argue,

42
00:01:52,141 --> 00:01:54,292
and it doesn't promise a refund.

43
00:01:54,292 --> 00:01:57,450
It tells the caller a supervisor will call back

44
00:01:57,450 --> 00:01:59,063
within one business day,

45
00:01:59,063 --> 00:02:00,744
writes down what it said,

46
00:02:00,744 --> 00:02:02,558
and asks for the best time.

47
00:02:02,558 --> 00:02:05,717
We'll pick afternoon. A gas smell is different.

48
00:02:05,717 --> 00:02:07,128
That's a safety stop.

49
00:02:07,128 --> 00:02:09,884
The caller is told to leave the house and

50
00:02:09,884 --> 00:02:11,094
call nine one one,

51
00:02:11,094 --> 00:02:12,505
before anything else.

52
00:02:13,357 --> 00:02:14,694
On the business side,

53
00:02:14,694 --> 00:02:16,159
the handoff lands here.

54
00:02:16,159 --> 00:02:18,833
Each row is what the person who follows up

55
00:02:18,833 --> 00:02:20,552
needs. Why the caller came,

56
00:02:20,552 --> 00:02:22,335
exactly what they were told,

57
00:02:22,335 --> 00:02:24,054
and the window they picked.

58
00:02:24,054 --> 00:02:26,983
So nobody makes the caller repeat their story.

59
00:02:27,835 --> 00:02:30,484
The overview tracks the success metric,

60
00:02:30,484 --> 00:02:32,317
calls settled by the agent,

61
00:02:32,317 --> 00:02:35,985
against the sixty to seventy-five percent target band,

62
00:02:35,985 --> 00:02:38,837
with volume, errors and reply times below.

63
00:02:38,837 --> 00:02:41,689
Today, that's mostly our own test traffic.

64
00:02:41,689 --> 00:02:43,727
And this is the learning loop.

65
00:02:43,727 --> 00:02:46,511
Any conversation can be flagged as wrong,

66
00:02:46,511 --> 00:02:49,092
and turned into a draft test scenario.

67
00:02:49,092 --> 00:02:52,216
A person writes the right answer and fixes the

68
00:02:52,216 --> 00:02:54,185
document or the instructions.

69
00:02:54,185 --> 00:02:56,562
Then we rerun the eval and compare.

70
00:02:57,414 --> 00:02:59,173
What the eval numbers say.

71
00:02:59,173 --> 00:03:00,391
On the graded run,

72
00:03:00,391 --> 00:03:04,181
projected containment is twenty-six point eight percent.

73
00:03:04,181 --> 00:03:08,106
Warranty and billing contained neither of their scenarios.

74
00:03:08,106 --> 00:03:11,827
Accuracy on the ten handled-driver scenarios is four of

75
00:03:11,827 --> 00:03:14,872
ten, and a person's grades match the judge on

76
00:03:14,872 --> 00:03:18,323
all ten. All fourteen scenarios that must leave the

77
00:03:18,323 --> 00:03:21,571
agent did: twelve handoffs and two safety stops.

78
00:03:21,571 --> 00:03:25,902
Thirty-one scenarios give a coarse projection with no confidence

79
00:03:25,902 --> 00:03:29,556
interval. A second run landed at thirty-six point five

80
00:03:29,556 --> 00:03:32,331
percent and disagreed on seven scenarios.

81
00:03:32,331 --> 00:03:34,902
Both are under the sixty percent band.

82
00:03:35,754 --> 00:03:39,147
So, can it settle sixty to seventy-five percent?

83
00:03:39,147 --> 00:03:40,632
Not on this evidence.

84
00:03:40,632 --> 00:03:44,096
The projection is twenty-six point eight percent,

85
00:03:44,096 --> 00:03:45,793
and the misses are real.

86
00:03:45,793 --> 00:03:47,348
The handoffs did fire.

87
00:03:47,348 --> 00:03:48,762
Thanks for watching.
